This patent grant is subject to the same conditions and termination
rules as the copyright grant. It grants no independent right to sell,
commercially operate, or otherwise commercially exploit a covered work.
Any patent permission necessary for Commercial Use must be covered by
appropriate separate authorization from parties entitled to grant it.

  Here, a "patent license" includes an express permission, covenant not
to sue, or other express commitment not to enforce a patent. If you
knowingly rely on such a license when conveying a covered work, you
must ensure that recipients can lawfully exercise the rights granted
by this License and can obtain the Corresponding Source free of charge
as required by sections 4 and 6. "Knowingly rely" means actual knowledge
that, absent the patent license, the conveyance or permitted use would
infringe identifiable patent claims you have reason to believe valid.

  If you convey a covered work and grant some recipients a patent
license for activities permitted under this License, that patent grant
must extend to all recipients for those same permitted activities.
This does not automatically extend a separately negotiated commercial
